{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Jonathan Lloyd — Human Datastream",
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "description": "Summarised biometric and cognitive metrics for Jonathan Lloyd, composed on data-change events by a backend Lambda and served as LLM-optimized markdown alongside canonical JSON.\n\nThe path carries the major version: v1. Within a version, response schemas only gain optional members. A removed member or a changed type ships as a new path version, and the old version keeps answering for at least 90 days. During that period its responses carry the Deprecation and Sunset headers and a Link header with rel=\"successor-version\". A major release of the portal contract that removes or retypes an export member triggers a new version.\n\nEach client gets 60 requests per minute. Every response from an export path under /api/v1 carries the RateLimit-Policy header field from the IETF httpapi draft, and every response the counter counted also carries the RateLimit header field. If the counter is unavailable, the request is still served and the RateLimit field is absent. A 429 response also carries Retry-After. The limit is a courtesy budget for a free, read-only API."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://jonathanlloyd.me/api/v1",
      "description": "The API base is https://jonathanlloyd.me/api/v1, and https://jonathanlloyd.me/openapi.json lists the nine export paths under it."
    }
  ],
